From: XinnorLab <135218967+XinnorLab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:48:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] feat(placement): placement_build row and the
 admit-latency histogram

`config show` reports the build facts in every mode --
`placement_build = wrr=<0|1> connector=<0|1> prealloc=<0|1>` -- so the
Stage C helper compares them across MDS instead of reading journals
(ENABLE_DS_PREALLOC now sets a compile definition like the connector
option does).  `pnfs_mds_placement_admit_seconds` (the upstream 12-bucket
histogram with _sum/_count) is observed once per placement_select_gated
call in every mode, legacy included, and once per
placement_gate_admit_create, so the LAT-25 row measures the gate alone.
Design spec section 9 (Stage C additions).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
